 "research": "Standing on the right leg, left leg works; trunk upright, hands on fixed handles in front (elev 25, plane 85, elbow 70). Thigh stays vertical (knee joint fixed): start leg straight-ish (ankle 0.89 m below the hip, knee ~14 deg), roller behind the lower shin; end knee ~100 deg (shin past horizontal: ankle = knee + 0.45 (0, sin100, -cos100)), foot relaxed (rot X +100 keeps it square to the shin). The roller rides the back of the shin (t 0.86 knee->ankle) on a lever whose pivot sits beside the knee joint, so the lever keeps its length. Only the left (working) side is lit. Bourne 2017 (leg curl EMG), Maeo 2021 (hip angle and hamstring length).",
